{
  "_about": "FlowShield design tokens: the single source for colours shared by the desktop app and the website. Edit this file, then run `python tools/build_tokens.py` to regenerate DesktopApp/Styles/Tokens.xaml, DesktopApp/Styles/Tokens.Light.xaml and the marked colour blocks in Website/styles.css. A tier 5 test fails if the generated files are out of date. See DESIGN_SYSTEM.md, sections 2 and 14.",

  "_format": "A colour is either a hex string, or {\"ref\": <other token>, \"alpha\": 0..1}. Tokens under css_only are copied into the CSS as-is and have no app equivalent.",

  "_depth": "From mica down, the depth system of the November 2026 redesign (DESIGN_SYSTEM.md Part A, design/redesign-2026-11/README.md): E0 mica (with its solid fallback), the E1/E2/E3 elevations and the acrylic tint, top highlights, hairlines, raised controls, recessed wells, and the gradient stops of the Primary button, the ring and the sprint glow. white is a base for the translucent highlights and is not emitted on its own.",

